WEBVTT

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:04.032
Three pendulums swing
inside a moving carriage.

00:00:04.328 --> 00:00:06.488
Can you reconstruct what moved them?

00:00:06.992 --> 00:00:13.232
On each run, a controller selects one of
three motion profiles for each event.

00:00:13.537 --> 00:00:17.809
All three travel the same
distance. Their timing differs.

00:00:18.192 --> 00:00:24.624
The camera travels with the carriage. Each exposure
catches the pendulums after a translation.

00:00:25.015 --> 00:00:30.151
Seven photographs record the initial
state and six successive events.

00:00:30.473 --> 00:00:35.081
The controller chose B, C, B, A, B, A.

00:00:35.738 --> 00:00:40.082
GPT-6.1 Sol recovered this whole sequence.

00:00:40.412 --> 00:00:47.396
CaveBench asks 1,180 questions across twenty
apparatuses in five physical domains.

00:00:47.988 --> 00:00:55.140
Across all six-event questions, Sol
recovered 1,035 of 1,200 individual events.

00:00:55.708 --> 00:01:02.188
Requiring every event to match gives
136 correct sequences out of 200.

00:01:02.597 --> 00:01:07.967
On 200 six-event questions,
SFT got 40 completely right,

00:01:07.967 --> 00:01:13.709
while two SimPO runs with different
seeds got 63 and 64 completely right.

00:01:14.180 --> 00:01:19.676
Both runs correctly answered the
same 26 questions that SFT missed.

